  "dimensions": [
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_87a0a594",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: Hateful; overall-intent-description: The meme juxtaposes a quote from Barack Obama condemning attacks on Muslims with a stock image of a cowboy stating a similar sentiment about Americans. The intent is to draw an analogy suggesting that attacking one American is equivalent to attacking all Americans, implying that the same logic should apply to Muslims. This is a hateful meme because it uses the image of a white American cowboy to implicitly equate the concept of 'attacking one American' with the idea of 'attacking all Americans,' which is a dangerous and exclusionary framing. It promotes the idea that Muslims are not 'Americans' and that the same logic of 'one person = all' does not apply to them, which is a form of Islamophobia. The meme is designed to provoke division and reinforce harmful stereotypes by suggesting that Muslims are not fully part of the American identity, thereby justifying potential discrimination or violence against them. The use of the cowboy image, often associated with white, rural, and traditional American identity, further reinforces the implicit racial and cultural hierarchy in the meme's message, making it a hateful and potentially harmful piece of content.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_65889dca"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
